{"name":"Cupid","hex":"#f5b2c5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cupid","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The god of love, son of Venus; sometimes depicted as a putto (a naked, winged boy with bow and arrow). The Roman counterpart of Eros.","Sudden love or desire; the personification of falling in love."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cupid"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cupid","blocks":[{"text":"In classical mythology, Cupid is the god of desire, erotic love, attraction and affection. He is often portrayed as the son of the love goddess Venus and the god of war Mars. He is also known as Amor. His Greek counterpart is Eros.\nAlthough Eros is generally portrayed as a slender winged youth in Classical Greek art, during the Hellenistic period, he was increasingly portrayed as a chubby boy. During this time, his iconography acquired the bow and arrow that represent his source of power: a person, or even a deity, who is shot by Cupid's arrow is filled with uncontrollable desire. In myths, Cupid is a minor character who serves mostly to set the plot in motion. He is a main character only in the tale of Cupid and Psyche, in which he is wounded by his own weapons and experiences the ordeal of love. Although other extended stories are not told about him, his tradition is rich in poetic themes and visual scenarios, such as \"Love conquers all\" and the retaliatory punishment or torture of Cupid."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Bertel_Thorvaldsen_-_Cupid.jpg/330px-Bertel_Thorvaldsen_-_Cupid.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cupid"},{"title":"Cupid (Fifty Fifty song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Cupid\" is a song recorded by South Korean girl group Fifty Fifty. It was released as The Beginning: Cupid, a single album featuring a Korean version, an English version sung by group members Sio and Aran, and an instrumental version of the song, on February 24, 2023, through Attrakt. It is a K-pop, disco-pop, synth-pop, and bubblegum song about a young girl's unrequited love and the shame she feels because of it."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a6/Fifty_Fifty_-_The_Beginning_Cupid.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cupid_(Fifty_Fifty_song)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Duquesnoy_Cupid_prewar_photo.jpg/500px-Duquesnoy_Cupid_prewar_photo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Duquesnoy_Cupid_prewar_photo.jpg/500px-Duquesnoy_Cupid_prewar_photo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cupid Carving His Bow (1620s) by François Duquesnoy, Bode Museum, Berlin","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADuquesnoy_Cupid_prewar_photo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Piero_della_Francesca_-_Cupid_Blindfolded_-_WGA17587.jpg/500px-Piero_della_Francesca_-_Cupid_Blindfolded_-_WGA17587.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Piero_della_Francesca_-_Cupid_Blindfolded_-_WGA17587.jpg/500px-Piero_della_Francesca_-_Cupid_Blindfolded_-_WGA17587.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A blindfolded, armed Cupid (1452/66) by Piero della Francesca","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APiero_della_Francesca_-_Cupid_Blindfolded_-_WGA17587.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Edme_Bouchardon%2C_Cupid%2C_1744%2C_NGA_41708.jpg/250px-Edme_Bouchardon%2C_Cupid%2C_1744%2C_NGA_41708.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/co